  "comments": "The standard weight of a sovereign was 160/623 troy ounce (123.3 grains). The pure gold content was 113 1/623 grains (7.3224 g).<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse, reverse and overdate varieties exist:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM#736.1</span> Without die number;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM#736.2</span> Die number below wreath (the main photograph);<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">KM#736.3</span> Additional raised line on lower part of ribbon (Ansell type).<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">A die error is known to exist:</span><br />\r\nObverse with &quot;GRΛTIΛ&quot; instead of &quot;GRATIA&quot;:<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d9babcd82dba.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d9babcd82dba.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" /></a><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">© Image courtesy of Dix Noonan Webb (www.dnw.co.uk)</span><br /><br />\r\nNote: for issues with mintmark below wreath, see <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/australia_colonial-1.html#c_australia_colonial8339\">Australia - Colonial</a><br />\r\n(M = Melbourne mint, S = Sydney mint)",
